{"id":"mahabharata-5-133","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":133,"title":"त्रयस्त्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 133 · Sanjaya answers his mother","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya says his mother's heart is like iron, and asks what use the kingdom would be to her if he died. Vidula replies that a mother does not bear sons to live in shame, and she tells him the arts of winning allies, of not trusting enemies and of rallying supporters.","kn":"ತಾಯಿಯ ಹೃದಯ ಕಬ್ಬಿಣದಂತೆ, ತಾನು ಸತ್ತರೆ ಅವಳಿಗೆ ರಾಜ್ಯದಿಂದೇನು ಪ್ರಯೋಜನ ಎಂದು ಸಂಜಯನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತಾಯಿ ಅವಮಾನದಲ್ಲಿ ಬದುಕಲು ಮಕ್ಕಳನ್ನು ಹೆರುವುದಿಲ್ಲ ಎಂದು ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ವಿದುಲೆ ಮಿತ್ರರನ್ನು ಗಳಿಸುವ, ಶತ್ರುಗಳನ್ನು ನಂಬದಿರುವ, ಬೆಂಬಲಿಗರನ್ನು ಕೂಡಿಸುವ ಕಲೆಗಳನ್ನು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"सञ्जय कहता है कि माता का हृदय लोहे जैसा है, और पूछता है कि यदि वह मर गया तो राज्य उनके किस काम का। विदुला उत्तर देती है कि माता लज्जा में जीने के लिए पुत्र नहीं जनती, और उसे मित्र बनाने, शत्रुओं पर विश्वास न करने और समर्थकों को जुटाने की कलाएँ बताती है।","te":"తల్లి హృదయం ఇనుము వంటిదని, తాను చనిపోతే రాజ్యం వల్ల ఆమెకు ఏమి ప్రయోజనమని సంజయుడు అడుగుతాడు. తల్లి అవమానంతో బ్రతకడానికి కుమారులను కనదని బదులిచ్చి విదుల మిత్రులను సంపాదించే, శత్రువులను నమ్మకపోయే, మద్దతుదారులను కూడగట్టే కళలను చెబుతుంది.","ta":"அன்னையின் உள்ளம் இரும்பு போன்றது, நான் இறந்தால் அரசால் உனக்கென்ன பயன் என்று ஸஞ்ஜயன் கேட்கிறான். அவமானத்தில் வாழத் தாய் மைந்தர்களைப் பெறுவதில்லை என்று பதிலளித்து விதுலை நண்பர்களைப் பெறுவது, பகைவரை நம்பாதிருப்பது, ஆதரவாளர்களைத் திரட்டுவது பற்றிய நுட்பங்களைச் சொல்கிறாள்.","ml":"അമ്മയുടെ ഹൃദയം ഇരുമ്പുപോലെയാണെന്ന് സഞ്ജയൻ പറയുന്നു; താൻ മരിച്ചാൽ രാജ്യം കൊണ്ട് അമ്മയ്ക്ക് എന്ത് പ്രയോജനമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം ചോദിക്കുന്നു. അപമാനത്തിൽ ജീവിക്കാനല്ല അമ്മ മക്കളെ പ്രസവിക്കുന്നതെന്ന് വിദുല മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു; സഖ്യകക്ഷികളെ നേടാനും, ശത്രുക്കളെ വിശ്വസിക്കാതിരിക്കാനും, പിന്തുണക്കാരെ ഒരുമിപ്പിക്കാനുമുള്ള വിദ്യകൾ അവൾ പറഞ്ഞുകൊടുക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.133; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"पुत्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The son said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"कृष्णायसस्येव च ते संहत्य हृदयं कृतम् ।\nमम मातस्त्वकरुणे वैरप्रज्ञे ह्यमर्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mother, your heart seems forged of black iron welded together: you are merciless, bent on enmity, and without tenderness."}},{"n":2,"text":"अहो क्षत्रसमाचारो यत्र मामपरं यथा ।\nईदृशं वचनं ब्रूयाद्भवती पुत्रमेकजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alas, the way of kshatriyas, that you would speak such words to your only son, as though I were a stranger."}},{"n":3,"text":"किं नु ते मामपश्यन्त्याः पृथिव्या अपि सर्वया ।\nकिमाभरणकृत्यं ते किं भोगैर्जीवितेन वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you were not to see me, what would even the whole earth be to you? What use are ornaments, pleasures or life itself?"}},{"text":"मातोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The mother said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"सर्वारम्भा हि विदुषां तात धर्मार्थकारणात् ।\nतानेवाभिसमीक्ष्याहं संजय त्वामचूचुदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son, all the undertakings of the wise are for the sake of dharma and wealth. Considering just those two, Sanjaya, I have urged you on."}},{"n":5,"text":"स समीक्ष्यक्रमोपेतो मुख्यः कालोऽयमागतः ।\nअस्मिंश्चेदागते काले कार्यं न प्रतिपद्यसे ।\nअसंभावितरूपस्त्वं सुनृशंसं करिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This chief moment has come, with all the right conditions. If you do not act when this time has come, you who were not thought capable of it will do something very cruel."}},{"n":6,"text":"तं त्वामयशसा स्पृष्टं न ब्रूयां यदि संजय ।\nखरीवात्सल्यमाहुस्तन्निःसामर्थ्यमहेतुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I did not speak to you now, touched as you are by disgrace, Sanjaya, that would be what they call a she-ass's fondness: powerless and pointless."}},{"n":7,"text":"सद्भिर्विगर्हितं मार्गं त्यज मूर्खनिषेवितम् ।\nअविद्या वै महत्यस्ति यामिमां संश्रिताः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leave the path condemned by the good and followed by fools. There is a great ignorance in which people take refuge."}},{"n":8,"text":"तव स्याद्यदि सद्वृत्तं तेन मे त्वं प्रियो भवेः ।\nधर्मार्थगुणयुक्तेन नेतरेण कथंचन ।\nदैवमानुषयुक्तेन सद्भिराचरितेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"If your conduct is good, then you will be dear to me, through conduct that has dharma, wealth and good qualities, divine and human help, and that is practiced by the good, never otherwise."}},{"n":9,"text":"यो ह्येवमविनीतेन रमते पुत्रनप्तृणा ।\nअनुत्थानवता चापि मोघं तस्य प्रजाफलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who delights in an undisciplined son or grandson, one who makes no effort, has a fruitless line of descendants."}},{"n":10,"text":"अकुर्वन्तो हि कर्माणि कुर्वन्तो निन्दितानि च ।\nसुखं नैवेह नामुत्र लभन्ते पुरुषाधमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who do no work, or who do blameworthy work, the lowest of men, find no happiness here or beyond."}},{"n":11,"text":"युद्धाय क्षत्रियः सृष्टः संजयेह जयाय च ।\nक्रूराय कर्मणे नित्यं प्रजानां परिपालने ।\nजयन्वा वध्यमानो वा प्राप्नोतीन्द्रसलोकताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, the kshatriya is made for battle and victory, always for harsh deeds and the protection of the people. Winning or being slain, he reaches Indra's world."}},{"n":12,"text":"न शक्रभवने पुण्ये दिवि तद्विद्यते सुखम् ।\nयदमित्रान्वशे कृत्वा क्षत्रियः सुखमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the holy palace of Shakra in heaven there is no happiness like what a kshatriya finds when he has brought his enemies under his power."}},{"n":13,"text":"मन्युना दह्यमानेन पुरुषेण मनस्विना ।\nनिकृतेनेह बहुशः शत्रून्प्रतिजिगीषया ॥","meaning":{"en":"A proud man who has been wronged again and again and burns with anger, wishing to defeat his enemies here,"}},{"n":14,"text":"आत्मानं वा परित्यज्य शत्रून्वा विनिपात्य वै ।\nअतोऽन्येन प्रकारेण शान्तिरस्य कुतो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"may find peace only by giving up himself or by felling his enemies. By what other way could he have peace?"}},{"n":15,"text":"इह प्राज्ञो हि पुरुषः स्वल्पमप्रियमिच्छति ।\nयस्य स्वल्पं प्रियं लोके ध्रुवं तस्याल्पमप्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A wise man here wishes only a little of what he dislikes; one who finds little to love in the world will surely meet only a little of what he dislikes."}},{"n":16,"text":"प्रियाभावाच्च पुरुषो नैव प्राप्नोति शोभनम् ।\nध्रुवं चाभावमभ्येति गत्वा गङ्गेव सागरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without anything dear a man gains nothing fine, and certainly ends in ruin, as the Ganga goes to the sea."}},{"text":"पुत्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The son said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"नेयं मतिस्त्वया वाच्या मातः पुत्रे विशेषतः ।\nकारुण्यमेवात्र पश्य भूत्वेह जडमूकवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mother, you should not say such a thing, especially to your son. Look for pity here, as if you were dull and dumb."}},{"text":"मातोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The mother said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अतो मे भूयसी नन्दिर्यदेवमनुपश्यसि ।\nचोद्यं मां चोदयस्येतद्भृशं वै चोदयामि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"It gives me greater joy that you see it so. You urge me to urge you, and I urge you strongly."}},{"n":19,"text":"अथ त्वां पूजयिष्यामि हत्वा वै सर्वसैन्धवान् ।\nअहं पश्यामि विजयं कृत्स्नं भाविनमेव ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I will honor you after you have slain all the Saindhavas. I see your complete victory as sure to come."}},{"text":"पुत्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The son said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"अकोशस्यासहायस्य कुतः स्विद्विजयो मम ।\nइत्यवस्थां विदित्वेमामात्मनात्मनि दारुणाम् ।\nराज्याद्भावो निवृत्तो मे त्रिदिवादिव दुष्कृतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can I win, without a treasury and without allies? Having seen this harsh state of mine, my wish for the kingdom has turned away, as if from heaven through evil deeds."}},{"n":21,"text":"ईदृशं भवती कंचिदुपायमनुपश्यति ।\nतन्मे परिणतप्रज्ञे सम्यक्प्रब्रूहि पृच्छते ।\nकरिष्यामि हि तत्सर्वं यथावदनुशासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you see some means for this, wise lady, tell me properly, for I ask; I will do all that you instruct exactly."}},{"text":"मातोवाच","meaning":{"en":"The mother said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"पुत्रात्मा नावमन्तव्यः पूर्वाभिरसमृद्धिभिः ।\nअभूत्वा हि भवन्त्यर्था भूत्वा नश्यन्ति चापरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son, do not think little of yourself because of earlier failures. Wealth comes where it was not, and others once had is lost."}},{"n":23,"text":"अमर्षेणैव चाप्यर्था नारब्धव्याः सुबालिशैः ।\nसर्वेषां कर्मणां तात फले नित्यमनित्यता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fools should not begin ventures out of mere anger. Every result of every act is always uncertain, my child."}},{"n":24,"text":"अनित्यमिति जानन्तो न भवन्ति भवन्ति च ।\nअथ ये नैव कुर्वन्ति नैव जातु भवन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing that results are uncertain, some people succeed and some do not; but those who do not act at all never succeed."}},{"n":25,"text":"ऐकगुण्यमनीहायामभावः कर्मणां फलम् ।\nअथ द्वैगुण्यमीहायां फलं भवति वा न वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without effort there is a single outcome: no result. With effort the outcome is double: it may or may not come."}},{"n":26,"text":"यस्य प्रागेव विदिता सर्वार्थानामनित्यता ।\nनुदेद्वृद्धिसमृद्धी स प्रतिकूले नृपात्मज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Prince, one who knows beforehand that all gains are uncertain should push on, whether success or setback lies ahead."}},{"n":27,"text":"उत्थातव्यं जागृतव्यं योक्तव्यं भूतिकर्मसु ।\nभविष्यतीत्येव मनः कृत्वा सततमव्यथैः ।\nमङ्गलानि पुरस्कृत्य ब्राह्मणैश्चेश्वरैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should rise, stay alert and engage in works for prosperity, always keeping the mind firm that it will succeed and unshaken, putting auspicious rites first, with brahmins and powerful men."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्राज्ञस्य नृपतेराशु वृद्धिर्भवति पुत्रक ।\nअभिवर्तति लक्ष्मीस्तं प्राचीमिव दिवाकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the wise king, my son, prosperity comes quickly. Fortune approaches him as the sun approaches the east."}},{"n":29,"text":"निदर्शनान्युपायांश्च बहून्युद्धर्षणानि च ।\nअनुदर्शितरूपोऽसि पश्यामि कुरु पौरुषम् ।\nपुरुषार्थमभिप्रेतं समाहर्तुमिहार्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have shown you many examples, means and spurs to courage. I see you now enlightened; show manhood. You should bring about here the aim a man seeks."}},{"n":30,"text":"क्रुद्धाँल्लुब्धान्परिक्षीणानवक्षिप्तान्विमानितान् ।\nस्पर्धिनश्चैव ये केचित्तान्युक्त उपधारय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Consider those who are angry, greedy, depleted, slighted or insulted, and any rivals, and use them with care."}},{"n":31,"text":"एतेन त्वं प्रकारेण महतो भेत्स्यसे गणान् ।\nमहावेग इवोद्धूतो मातरिश्वा बलाहकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this way you will break up great hosts, as a mighty storm wind scatters clouds."}},{"n":32,"text":"तेषामग्रप्रदायी स्याः कल्योत्थायी प्रियंवदः ।\nते त्वां प्रियं करिष्यन्ति पुरो धास्यन्ति च ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be the first to give to them, rise early for them, and speak kindly. They will do you kindness and will surely put you in front."}},{"n":33,"text":"यदैव शत्रुर्जानीयात्सपत्नं त्यक्तजीवितम् ।\nतदैवास्मादुद्विजते सर्पाद्वेश्मगतादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The moment an enemy knows his rival has given up on his life, he is afraid of him as of a snake in his house."}},{"n":34,"text":"तं विदित्वा पराक्रान्तं वशे न कुरुते यदि ।\nनिर्वादैर्निर्वदेदेनमन्ततस्तद्भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once he knows such a man to be bold and does not bring him under control, the end will be that he will be cast out by reproaches."}},{"n":35,"text":"निर्वादादास्पदं लब्ध्वा धनवृद्धिर्भविष्यति ।\nधनवन्तं हि मित्राणि भजन्ते चाश्रयन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"From being cast out you will find a footing, and wealth will grow. Friends serve and cling to the wealthy."}},{"n":36,"text":"स्खलितार्थं पुनस्तात संत्यजन्त्यपि बान्धवाः ।\nअप्यस्मिन्नाश्रयन्ते च जुगुप्सन्ति च तादृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But, child, even kinsmen leave one who has failed in his aim, though they cling to him again and scorn one like that."}},{"n":37,"text":"शत्रुं कृत्वा यः सहायं विश्वासमुपगच्छति ।\nअतः संभाव्यमेवैतद्यद्राज्यं प्राप्नुयादिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who makes an enemy his helper and trusts him: from this it is quite possible that he gains the kingdom."}}]}]}